    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a busy Tuesday slate with **Kyle Tucker** (73.73) and **Andy Pages** (68.03) anchoring the outfield as our premier starts. Both benefit significantly from favorable park factors and middle-of-the-order protection against Gallen, whose 4.36 xERA provides a target-rich environment. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.40) maintains a high floor in the three-hole, his output is slightly dampened by a dynamic platoon disadvantage; however, his elite xwOBA metrics make him a non-negotiable cornerstone today. **Sam Antonacci** remains a critical utility play (54.78); despite a middling matchup against Bradley, his status as a leadoff hitter and his superior 0.372 xwOBA underscore his value in a category-scarcity league that prioritizes high-frequency opportunities.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Miguel Vargas** on the bench with a 51.38 efficiency rating. While his hitting profile is competitive, he was edged out by the superior platoon alignment of **Coby Mayo** and the high-order density provided by **Josh Jung** and **Andy Pages**. Similarly, we are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (38.94); despite his utility, the combination of a daunting matchup against S\u00e1nchez and his bottom-third placement in the order drops him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold for active roster status. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Josh Lowe** for future rotations, as their speed profiles remain essential for our stolen base targets. Today\u2019s lineup remains high-risk where we face elite arm-talent like S\u00e1nchez, so expect volatility as we balance the game cap constraints against these specific matchup projections.",
